From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:17:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: mtk_dsi: Run the link at the peripheral's HS
 rate

mtk_dsi derives the HS lane rate from the mode's pixel clock alone. Some
panels need a faster link than their pixel data: the Zinwa Q25's 720x720
panel only locks at 652 Mbit/s per lane, about 25% above what its timing
needs on two lanes, so its driver had to inflate the pixel clock and the
horizontal front porch to get that rate, and the mode no longer described
the refresh rate the panel runs at.

Use the attached device's hs_rate when it is above the rate the pixel
data needs. The DSI engine times the frame in video mode, so the mode's
porches and the link rate then set the refresh rate.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index d86cc994..221b2c05 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -212,6 +212,7 @@ struct mtk_dsi {
 	struct clk *hs_clk;
 
 	u32 data_rate;
+	unsigned long hs_rate;
 
 	unsigned long mode_flags;
 	enum mipi_dsi_pixel_format format;
@@ -691,6 +692,9 @@ static int mtk_dsi_poweron(struct mtk_dsi *dsi)
 
 	dsi->data_rate = DIV_ROUND_UP_ULL(dsi->vm.pixelclock * bit_per_pixel,
 					  dsi->lanes);
+	/* A peripheral that needs a faster link than its pixel data names it. */
+	if (dsi->hs_rate > dsi->data_rate)
+		dsi->data_rate = dsi->hs_rate;
 
 	ret = clk_set_rate(dsi->hs_clk, dsi->data_rate);
 	if (ret < 0) {
@@ -993,6 +997,7 @@ static int mtk_dsi_host_attach(struct mipi_dsi_host *host,
 	dsi->lanes = device->lanes;
 	dsi->format = device->format;
 	dsi->mode_flags = device->mode_flags;
+	dsi->hs_rate = device->hs_rate;
 	dsi->next_bridge = devm_drm_of_get_bridge(dev, dev->of_node, 1, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(dsi->next_bridge)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(dsi->next_bridge);
